+/// `v1-asm-search-sum` (round 9, secure-only; the FSBL never names it): the WOTS+C count
+/// search with the digit sum in the driver. Per try the loop does what `v1_search_asm` does
+/// (DCIS poll with a 2^24 guard, HR3..HR7, SR clear; for a next try BUSY wait with a 2^24
+/// guard and stale-DCIS refusal, INIT, the 32 words, DCAL), but instead of calling `pred`
+/// it parks the raw HR3..HR7 words in the staging array during the block-0 window and, in the
+/// engine window, computes the exact digit sum of the low 129 bits (the round-7 v2 fold sum:
+/// spec 0.3 uses v1's digit position) with the same exact early reject (digits 32..42 add at
+/// most 77). Returns `(c, flag)` as `v1_search_asm`. `st`: 0..20 message words, 34 target,
+/// 40..45 the parked HR words.
+#[cfg(feature = "v1-asm-search-sum")]
+const V1SS_SPIN: u32 = 2;
+
+#[cfg(all(feature = "v1-asm-search-sum", not(all(feature = "tick-hook", not(feature = "tick-batch")))))]
+#[inline(always)]
+fn v1_search_sum_asm(st: *mut u32, start: u32, end: u32) -> (u32, u32) {
